# Implementation Plan - Merge StressSense & StressDetect

Merge the behavioral interaction tracking features and survey options from the StressDetect application into the Compose-based StressSense application, adding a PSS-10 Questionnaire screen, enhanced history graphs with scan-type filtering, a local Privacy Policy screen, and compiling the final Android APK.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **PSS-10 Questionnaire Scoring & Database Mapping:** 
> The PSS-10 survey is a 10-question test scored on a 0–40 scale. To merge this into the existing `StressScan` database schema (which uses a 0–100 scale for `finalScore` to drive all home metrics/graphs), we propose:
> 1. Scaling the raw PSS-10 score to a 0–100 scale in the database via `(rawScore * 2.5).toInt()`.
> 2. Setting the `scanType` field to `"QUESTIONNAIRE"`.
> 3. Displaying both the raw PSS score (e.g., `Score: 28/40`) and the scaled stress level in the history item details.

> [!NOTE]
> **Compilation Environment:**
> We have verified that the workspace includes a local JDK 17 (`.tools/jdk-17`) and Android SDK (`.tools/android-sdk`). We will configure the gradle build to use this local JDK, compile the application, and package it as a debug APK.

